{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019KFUy5SZ5QHV4p2vaVPNHt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-484\"\n3\ttitle = \"Concern/hat references on SR and LLR rows and the generated component view: effective sets derived never copied, components.derived.toml generated, detail_doc retired (OI-32 ruled (d), 2026-08-20)\"\n4\tspecref = \"docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-32\"\n5\tworkstream = \"requirements\"\n6\tsr_refs = []\n7\tneeds = []\n8\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n9\tsafety_class = \"spine\"\n10\tpriority = 2\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Context\n14\t\n15\t**SLICES 1–5 LANDED (2026-08-20, 2026-08-22, 2026-08-23 ×3) — the row is\n16\tACTIVE, not complete.** Phases 0, 1, 2, 3 and 5 have shipped; phase 4's\n17\tBLOCKER is resolved (WI-511, 2026-08-23) but the phase itself still awaits the\n18\towner's `hats.toml` value pass. What is still owed, in the order it should be\n19\ttaken: item 3 (owner-adjacent), item 5 (phase 4, now waiting on the owner\n20\trather than a mechanism) and item 7 (recorded, owed by nobody yet).\n21\t\n22\t1. ~~**Phase 2's judgement backfill.**~~ **DONE, slice 2 (2026-08-22)** — record:\n23\t   `docs/log.d/2026-08-22-wi484-hatrefs-backfill.md`. **55 SR cells and 8 LLR\n24\t   own refs** written by per-row judgement, against one stated rule (attribute a\n25\t   hat only where THAT hat's own `listens_for` names a failure the row prevents\n26\t   — not \"which lens could be held up to it\", which with nine `always` hats\n27\t   fills every cell and means nothing). `hat_refs` now stands on 72 of 74 SRs\n28\t   and 9 of 171 LLRs; coverage moved **184 → 4 of 245** uncovered by effective\n29\t   set, and unattributed hats **5 → 1**. The two known poison rows were read\n30\t   individually and BOTH STAY EMPTY: `SR-015`'s refusal of `hat.PERFORMANCE`\n31\t   is argued and correct, and no other hat bears once the checker splits to\n32\t   `SR-157`; `SR-040`'s struck lenses are not resurrected because the row