the prose is now commentary.\n59\t4. ~~**Phase 3 — the generated component view.**~~ **DONE, slice 3\n60\t   (2026-08-23)** — record: `docs/log.d/2026-08-23-wi484-component-view.md`.\n61\t   `gen_components.py`, `docs/requirements/components.derived.toml`, its\n62\t   `[generated]` row, its `component-view` freshness step and its `WIRED` entry\n63\t   landed together (the wiring test was driven RED in both directions first),\n64\t   plus a `trunk_step.REGEN_STEPS` entry and the adopter surface. `detail_doc`\n65\t   is RETIRED: no live CMP row carried it, so nothing needed migrating; the\n66\t   column is gone from the template, both carrier maps, `PROCESS_OPTIONS.md` and\n67\t   the test fixtures. The three coverage edges were RE-MEASURED (the brief's\n68\t   counts had all moved) and answered IN THE OUTPUT: the **5** childless SRs\n69\t   (not 12, and all five now `Approved`) are one counted repo-wide `[unplaced]`\n70\t   list, with the view deliberately NOT distinguishing \"not yet decomposed\" from\n71\t   \"constraint over everything\" because no registry cell does and a per-repo\n72\t   list of never-members has no place in shipped machinery; the **7**\n73\t   multi-component SRs (not 6) appear in EVERY component they reach and in each\n74\t   one's `sr_shared_refs`; seams DO enter the view, with all **130** placed\n75\t   (**62** by tag, 68 by endpoint resolution through `trace_text.norm_module`)\n76\t   and an unplaceable one named rather than dropped. Spine acts, all `Drafted`\n77\t   on the standing precedent: `LLR-199`, `TC-195`, `IF-139`–`IF-143`.\n78\t\n79\t5. **Phase 4 — knowledge derived from concerns — has a blocker the brief did not\n80\t   know about.** `hats.py` enforced a STRICT unknown-key refusal\n81\t   (`REQUIRED_KEYS`, and `hats.py` raised on any extra key), and had no\n82\t   notion of an optional key: adding `knowledge` to the roster therefore either\n83\t   makes it MANDATORY on all 16 live rows and all 16 shipped-template rows, or\n84\t  