cell\n137\tresolving against `[hat.NAME]` rows is exactly the vocabulary hop that rule\n138\trefuses. The id space is the **roster NAMES**; the `C-SEC-2`-style clause\n139\tnumbering in eight rationale cells is prose that resolves nowhere, and it is NOT\n140\tpromoted to a second id space.\n141\t\n142\tExecutes OI-32's ruling — (d) THE GENERATED VIEW — per the combined brief's\n143\tsix phases (the brief is the row's recommendation cell; read it whole first):\n144\t\n145\t- **Phase 0** reconciles the two hat vocabularies and SETTLES THE FIELD NAME —\n146\t  the owner's word (2026-08-20) was \"hats_ref\", the brief proposed\n147\t  `concern_refs`; one name, ruled here, used everywhere.\n148\t- **Phase 1** adds the field on SR and LLR rows to say which hats bear on the\n149\t  row; an LLR's EFFECTIVE set is DERIVED (own refs + inherited), never copied.\n150\t- **Phase 2** decides who writes it and runs the backfill over the live rows.\n151\t- ~~**Phase 3**~~ **DONE** — generates `docs/requirements/components.derived.toml`\n152\t  via `gen_components.py`, declared in `docs/stack.ini` `[generated]`;\n153\t  `detail_doc` retired with it.\n154\t- **Phase 4** derives knowledge packs from concerns via a `knowledge` field on\n155\t  `hats.toml`.\n156\t- **Phase 5** is OI-33's surviving residue: the amend-without-flip-style guard\n157\t  — a row whose normative cells move while its concern refs do not is a\n158\t  finding.\n159\t\n160\tCoverage edges the brief said the execution must answer explicitly rather than\n161\tpaper over — ANSWERED at slice 3 against re-measured counts (5 childless SRs, 7\n162\tmulti-component, 62 of 130 tagged IF rows); see item 4 above. Standing\n163\tconstraint from OI-30 D3, honoured: a GENERATED file never carries an approval\n164\t(`human_approval_through`).\n165\t\n166\t**Sequencing, the owner's own note (2026-08-20):** the new field is NOT\n167\tanticipated to be an attested cell, so it can be tacked on AFTER the sitting\n168\twithout re-open